      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It happen with my avatar in desktop. I have a feature that move the Root T.y on the additive layer. It simulate playspace for none steam/6pt/vr user. The name plate and voice move and the capsule stay on the ground.\nSome said that my nameplate was in my body and other witness it really high sometime.\nFor my case, it might be the normalize float bug that cause it and late joiner yadiyada.\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/avatar-30/p/bug-float-on-a-radial-open-on-wrong-value-remotely\nFor testing you can try my prefab\nhttps://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15TezWr-srzR0kas_FPHrQjC7nPg5d7mb\nOr one of the avatar in the Quest Church.\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_109d439d-a56b-461e-8194-d5f4c706e602\nReset the avatar fix the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-19T23:56:40.344Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The position of the nameplate height is either too high or too low (inside the avatar), depending on OpenVR Advanced Settings placespace mover height before calibration.\nSteps to reproduce:\n- Be in full body tracking\n- Use playspace mover to move up (or move downwards), or have a miscalibrated playspace floor height\n- Calibrate avatar\n- Reset playspace or playspace move back to have feet properly on the floor\nObserved:\n- Other players in the instance will see the nameplate way above the avatar, or inside the avatar",
